  "body": "What happens: The release gate of the v0.20.0 cut fails in the app heavy lane (release, `--ignored`). The test `the_sample_as_imported_still_generates_both_operations` in `crates/app/tests/shared_face_bodies.rs` imports a sample model and generates its two operations. The generate step now refuses operation R1.\n\nEvidence (release branch head `182b7018a`, log `gate-logs/release-20261114-185541/12-app_heavy_lane_release_--ignored_.log`):\n\n```\nthread 'the_sample_as_imported_still_generates_both_operations' panicked at crates\\app\\tests\\shared_face_bodies.rs:40:9:\ngenerate refused: {\"content\":[{\"text\":\"generate: R1 - could not generate the toolpath: R1: nothing to machine: nothing to cut: the model fills the pocket at every level\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"isError\":true}\n```\n\nExpected: both operations generate, as they did when the test was added (commit `6726c1b81`).\n\nNot known: which merge caused the change. Candidates are the importer changes since v0.19.0 (PR 1671 turns an inward-wound closed body outward; PR 1576 and PR 1638 change the STEP importer) and the stock-source law changes.\n\nDone means: the cause is named, the test passes in release with `--ignored`, and a refusal that is correct is recorded with its reason rather than removed.\n",
